# CHANGELOG

## Unreleased

### Core infrastructure

- Resource entries in `config/resources.yml` (references, assemblies, exclusions,
  stratifications, comparison vcf/bed) may now be **local filesystem paths** (or
  `file://` URIs) in addition to URLs, enabling offline / external use (GitLab
  #186). A shared `scripts/fetch_resource.sh` copies local files (decompressing by
  destination extension) or downloads remote URLs; schema no longer constrains
  these fields to `uri`/`url`.
- **Download retry logic**: `fetch_resource.sh` now retries remote downloads up to
  3 times with exponential backoff (5s → 10s delays), preventing pipeline failures
  from intermittent network errors.

### Bug fixes

- Fixed invalid escape sequence in `bench_vcf_normalize.smk` sed pattern that
  triggered Python SyntaxWarning.
- Documented known `snakemake --archive` network timeout issue when packaging conda
  environments; see `docs/issues/snakemake-archive-network-timeout.md` for
  workarounds.
- Updated `run_defrabb` help messages and CLAUDE.md to document rerun behavior and
  unlock command.

### Exclusions / benchmarks

- Added exclusion set `HG002Q100stvarv0.022` (HG002Q100stvarv0.017 minus
  `HG002Q100-mosaic`) for use by the next round of HG002Q100 stvar drafts;
  excluding mosaic regions unnecessarily fragmented the SV benchmark (GitLab
  #188). Dated analyses tables and the historical v0.016/v0.017 sets are left
  unchanged (each is tied to a released draft version).
- Self-discrepancy exclusions now drop symbolic/breakend ALT alleles (e.g. PAV
  `<INV>`) before hap.py, fixing the `Invalid allele ... <INV>` crash on SV
  benchmarks (GitLab #192). SV-aware self-discrepancy via Truvari remains tracked
  in #193.

### Evaluation

- `truvari bench` parameters are now configurable via named `truvari_bench_params`
  profiles in `config/resources.yml`, selected per-analysis through the
  analyses-table `eval_params` column (previously hardcoded). The `default`
  profile reproduces the prior parameters, so existing analyses are unchanged
  (GitLab #194). Supports pick/passonly/refdist/chunksize/pctseq/pctsize/pctovl/
  sizemin/sizemax/sizefilt/typeignore/dup_to_ins/bnddist.
- Added the `stvar_v5` truvari bench profile (`--pick ac --passonly -r 2000
  -C 5000 -B -1`) implementing the Truvari v5 recommendation for the Q100 SV
  benchmark from the Aug 2025 Illumina/NIST email thread (GitLab #194):
  `bnddist=-1` disables BND distance matching (the benchmark has no BNDs, so
  query BNDs would otherwise all score as FP). `--write-phab` is intentionally
  omitted, following the truvari v5 default for stable, comparison-set-independent
  baseline counts. New dev-round analyses tables should set `eval_params=stvar_v5`.
- Added **genome-specific stratifications** for hap.py smvar evaluations (GitLab
  #59 / #173). `scripts/genome_specific_strats.py` ports the GIAB
  genome-stratifications GenomeSpecific complex/overlapping-variant strata
  (comphetsnp / comphetindel / complexindel / snpswithin / othercomplex within
  10bp) — validated byte-identical to the upstream awk/bedtools pipeline on the
  HG002 chr21 dipcall VCF. `rules/stratifications_genome_specific.smk`
  (+ `envs/genome_strats.yml`) generates them from the draft benchmark VCF via
  `vcfgeno2haplo`. Opt-in: with config `genome_specific_strats: true`, `run_happy`
  merges the per-benchmark strata into the GIAB stratification TSV (default false
  leaves evaluations byte-identical). The SV/CNV stratum (GS rules 7-10) is
  designed but not yet wired; see `docs/issues/stratification-59-173-design.md`.
  `scripts/build_stratification_tsv.py` is the shared TSV builder/merger.
- Added `scripts/compare_evaluations.py`: a CLI that aggregates hap.py
  (`*.summary.csv`) and Truvari (`summary.json`, `refine.variant_summary.json`)
  results into a tidy precision/recall/F1 comparison table (Markdown + TSV), with
  `--baseline` deltas and regression/improvement flags for parameter
  optimization. Plotting via `scripts/plot_evaluations.R` (ggplot2;
  `envs/r_plot.yml`).

### Environments

- Restored `truvari anno remap` by installing a patched `bwapy` fork
  (`nate-d-olson/bwapy`) in `envs/truvari_remap.yml`; fixes the setuptools>=80
  build break and the `__log_finite` load failure on modern glibc (GitLab #200).

### CI / tooling

- CI now gates on `snakefmt --check` and `black --check` (scripts + .tests), and
  runs `snakemake --lint` as an advisory (non-blocking) job.

## Milestone v0.021 2026-04-16

Major release adding PAV as a second supported assembly variant caller,
introducing HG008 Normal/Tumor benchmark configurations, migrating the
test data S3 bucket, and consolidating release/report flow with a
dedicated stabilization pass.

### Variant calling

- Added PAV (Phased Assembly Variant caller) as an alternative to dipcall
  via the Apptainer container `becklab/pav`; new rules and configuration
  hooks under `rules/asm-varcall.smk` and supporting changes in
  `rules/exclusions.smk` and `rules/bench_vcf_processing.smk`
- Refactored PAV and dipcall rules to use standardized input/output
  paths so downstream rules can treat callers interchangeably
- Added PAV exclusion handling (PAV-vs-dipcall discrepancies, PAV
  callable-region intersection)
- Numerous PAV bug fixes: missing INFO field, region BED merging,
  baseline BED sorting, ambiguous name errors, long-runtime mitigations
  (skipping remap, removing repmask/smvar trfanno), inversion exclusions
- Fix `intersect_pav_callable_regions` to use the hap1 callable BED for
  `h1_bed` (was using the wrong bed)
- Fixed `run_pav` "FATAL FIPS SELFTEST FAILURE" on FIPS-enabled hosts. PAV's
  pip-installed pysam bundles a FIPS-capable OpenSSL that auto-enables FIPS when
  the host kernel is in FIPS mode and aborts on a failing self-test (not
  bypassable via `OPENSSL_CONF`). `run_defrabb` now detects a FIPS host and binds
  `/proc/sys/crypto/fips_enabled` -> `0` inside apptainer containers
  (`APPTAINER_BIND`), so the stock `becklab/pav:latest` image works unchanged;
  no-op on non-FIPS hosts. The PAV image is also now configurable via
  `_pav_container` in `config/resources.yml`. See
  `docs/issues/run_pav_fips_selftest.md`.

### Benchmarks and assemblies

- Added HG008 Normal/Tumor assemblies and analysis tables
  (`config/analyses_20250408_v0.021_HG008TN.tsv` through
  `config/analyses_20250708_v0.021_HG008TN.tsv`)
- Added HG002 v1.1 CI test configuration
  (`config/analyses_20260323_v0.020_HG002v1.1-CI.tsv`)
- Updated/curated 20250516 assemblies; HG008 assembly URL refreshes

### Test data S3 bucket migration

- Migrated test data resource URLs from the `giab-data/giab-test-data/`
  prefix to a dedicated `giab-test-data` bucket in `config/resources.yml`,
  so the test data is no longer affected by the bucket-wide
  Intelligent-Tiering rule on `giab-data`. Other resource URLs that live
  outside the `giab-test-data/` prefix (e.g., HG008N assemblies, NA12878
  palladium, external-evaluation callsets) remain in `giab-data`.
- Migration plan and archive-recovery procedures are kept under
  `docs/archive/` for historical reference

### Release flow and wrapper

- `run_defrabb` now respects configured release inputs instead of a
  hardcoded S3 bucket
- Apply include/exclude release filtering during S3 upload
- Ensure `data_manifest.tsv` is uploaded as part of the release flow;
  added to `config/release.json`
- Make the root `analysis.qmd` the canonical report source; removed the
  duplicate at `scripts/reports/analysis.qmd`

### Environments and tooling

- Updated Truvari version pin
- Conda mirror version bump and env updates for the remote source
- Streamlined mamba install command (channel priority consolidation)
- Added Apptainer dependency for PAV rules
- Updated `.gitignore` for PAV cache and result directories

### Documentation

- Added `docs/developer-quickstart.md` for a concise local setup +
  validation checklist
- Tracked previously-uncommitted reference docs:
  `docs/architecture-diagram.md` (Mermaid flowchart and ER diagram),
  `docs/development-roadmap.md` (phased refactoring plan),
  `docs/TODO-pre-development.md` (20-item prioritized checklist),
  `docs/claude-code-recommendations.md` (advisory),
  `docs/giab_test_data_new_bucket_migration_plan.md`,
  `docs/giab_test_data_s3_archive_recovery.md`
- Tracked per-tool agent guides at the repo root: `CLAUDE.md`,
  `AGENTS.md`, `GEMINI.md`
- Removed stale `.github/workflows/` (snakemake template artifacts —
  GitLab is the canonical CI)

### Tests

- Added `test_stabilization_pr.py` regression coverage for the
  stabilization pass

